; A double-quoted token in a value expression is an amount when a quantity
; follows the quoted commodity (#2172), and a string otherwise.  The quantity
; may carry a minus sign, with or without a space before it, as in a journal;
; a plus sign or comma after the closing quote is an operator (#3251).  The
; error cases are in expr-quoted-token-errors.test.

test eval '"ab"-1'
ab-1
end test

test eval '"ab" -1'
ab -1
end test

test eval '"ab"+1'
ab1
end test

test eval '"ab"'
ab
end test
